Fix HDMI-CEC on the Valve Steam Machine (Fremont).

cros-ec-cec looks up its CEC notifier by (hdmi_dev, port_name) using the
connector name from its DMI table, and Fremont's entry asks for "Port C".
amdgpu never names its connectors: amdgpu_dm_initialize_hdmi_connector()
calls cec_notifier_conn_register(hdmi_dev, NULL, &conn_info).

Since cec_notifier_conn_register() allocates a fresh notifier when the tuple
does not already exist, the named lookup creates a second, orphaned notifier.
amdgpu then publishes EDID and physical address changes to its own unnamed
notifier, which the adapter is not attached to, so the CEC adapter comes up
stuck at physical address f.f.f.f and can never claim a logical address:

    Connector Info   : None
    Physical Address : f.f.f.f
    Logical Address Mask : 0x0000

Port names are an i915/Chromebook convention. NULL is documented as correct
when the HDMI device has a single HDMI connector, which Fremont does.

The AMD Lilac and OEM F7F entries point at the same PCI device and likely
need the same treatment, but are left alone here as they are untested.

--- a/drivers/media/cec/platform/cros-ec/cros-ec-cec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/cec/platform/cros-ec/cros-ec-cec.c
@@ -306,6 +306,12 @@
 	const char *const *conns;
 };

+/*
+ * amdgpu registers its CEC notifier with no port name (see
+ * amdgpu_dm_initialize_hdmi_connector), so a named lookup allocates a second,
+ * orphaned notifier and the adapter never receives a physical address.
+ */
+static const char *const port_unnamed_conns[] = { NULL };
 static const char *const port_b_conns[] = { "Port B", NULL };
 static const char *const port_c_conns[] = { "Port C", NULL };
 static const char *const port_db_conns[] = { "Port D", "Port B", NULL };
@@ -318,7 +324,7 @@
 	{ "AMD", "Lilac", "0000:03:00.0", port_c_conns },
 	/* Valve Fremont */
 	{ "OEM", "F7F", "0000:03:00.0", port_c_conns },
-	{ "Valve", "Fremont", "0000:03:00.0", port_c_conns },
+	{ "Valve", "Fremont", "0000:03:00.0", port_unnamed_conns },
 	/* Google Fizz */
 	{ "Google", "Fizz", "0000:00:02.0", port_b_conns },
 	/* Google Brask */
